; A DebugValue without an active DebugScope must still be given a
; verifier-correct DILocation recovered from the variable itself. To do that,
; reverse translation needs the DISubprogram of the function currently being
; emitted (SPIRVToLLVMDbgTran::transDebugIntrinsic only recovers a location
; when the variable is scoped to that subprogram). While a function body is
; being translated its "dbg" metadata attachment is not set yet, so it cannot
; use Function::getSubprogram() and must fall back to FuncMap.
;
; This test exercises exactly that FuncMap fallback for the OpenCL.DebugInfo.100
; flavor: unlike NonSemantic.Shader.DebugInfo.*, a DebugFunction here carries
; the SPIR-V function id and eagerly drives body translation
; (transDebugFunction -> transFunctionBody -> SPIRVReader::transFunction),
; recursing into transDebugIntrinsic before the "dbg" attachment exists. foo
; calls bar so the bodies are translated through that recursive path. Two
; functions are used so the fallback must key FuncMap by the enclosing SPIR-V
; function id and resolve each scope-less DebugValue to the correct subprogram:
;  - "x" is scoped to bar and must be recovered against bar's subprogram.
;  - "c" is scoped to foo and must be recovered against foo's subprogram.
; A wrong lookup would either drop the record or trip the verifier's
; conflicting-argument check (x is arg 1 of bar).
;
; Both functions are plain spir_func (exported, no OpEntryPoint) so each
; DebugFunction maps one-to-one onto the emitted define; there is no kernel
; entry-point wrapper that could be merged into the debug-bearing function and
; blur which define the recovered records land in.

; RUN: llvm-spirv -to-binary %s -o %t.spv
; RUN: llvm-spirv -r %t.spv -o %t.rev.bc
; RUN: llvm-dis %t.rev.bc -o %t.rev.ll
; RUN: FileCheck < %t.rev.ll %s -check-prefix=CHECK-LLVM

; RUN: opt -passes=verify -disable-output %t.rev.bc 2>&1 \
; RUN:  | FileCheck %s --allow-empty --check-prefix=CHECK-VERIFY

; CHECK-LLVM: define spir_func i32 @bar(i32 %{{[0-9a-z]+}}){{.*}} !dbg ![[#BAR:]]
; CHECK-LLVM: #dbg_value(i32 %{{[0-9a-z]+}}, ![[#VARX:]], !DIExpression(), ![[#LOCX:]])
; CHECK-LLVM: define spir_func i32 @foo(i32 %{{[0-9a-z]+}}){{.*}} !dbg ![[#FOO:]]
; CHECK-LLVM: #dbg_value(i32 %{{[0-9a-z]+}}, ![[#VARC:]], !DIExpression(), ![[#LOCC:]])

; CHECK-LLVM-DAG: ![[#BAR]] = distinct !DISubprogram(name: "bar"
; CHECK-LLVM-DAG: ![[#FOO]] = distinct !DISubprogram(name: "foo"
; CHECK-LLVM-DAG: ![[#VARX]] = !DILocalVariable(name: "x", arg: 1, scope: ![[#BAR]]
; CHECK-LLVM-DAG: ![[#VARC]] = !DILocalVariable(name: "c", scope: ![[#FOO]]
; CHECK-LLVM-DAG: ![[#LOCX]] = !DILocation(line: 1, scope: ![[#BAR]])
; CHECK-LLVM-DAG: ![[#LOCC]] = !DILocation(line: 11, scope: ![[#FOO]])

; CHECK-VERIFY-NOT: invalid debug info
; CHECK-VERIFY-NOT: conflicting debug info
; CHECK-VERIFY-NOT: attachment points at wrong subprogram

